---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Sessions and context"
  description="Veasel Code sessions: SQLite history, repository map, adaptive compaction, prompt-cache accounting, parallel reads, durable jobs, and honest cost."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / SESSIONS</p>
    <h1>
      Long work.
      <br />
      <em>Measured context.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Sessions store messages and events in local SQLite. Compaction, repository
      map, prompt-cache accounting, parallel read-only tools, and durable async
      turns keep long work useful — without inventing provider savings or Harbor
      Index scores.
    </p>

    <div class="compatibility-banner">
      <span class="compatibility-mark" aria-hidden="true">
        ☷
      </span>
      <div>
        <strong>
          Compaction · map · cache · parallel reads · durable jobs
        </strong>
        <p>
          Measured <code>session.compaction</code> events, extractive{" "}
          <code>/map</code>, provider-reported cache counters when adapters set
          them, concurrent list/read/search with ordered transcript append, and{" "}
          <code>Prefer: respond-async</code> recovery after restart.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Local session store</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          Create a session by choosing an existing workspace directory. The
          canonical path is stored with the session.
        </li>
        <li>
          State and creation events write in one transaction. SSE events use
          monotonic IDs so clients can resume from a cursor.
        </li>
        <li>
          Chat messages are capped at 1 MiB (1,048,576 bytes) of text. That is
          not Muse’s advertised token context window.
        </li>
        <li>
          Fork a session with <code>POST /v1/sessions/{"{id}"}/fork</code> (or
          <code>/fork</code> in the TUI) to copy its history into a new session.
          Delete one with <code>DELETE /v1/sessions/{"{id}"}</code> or{" "}
          <code>d</code> twice in the Sessions dialog; deletion removes the
          session's stored state and never touches workspace files.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Repository map</h2>
      <p>
        An Aider-style extractive map ranks workspace files for context
        selection. In the TUI, run <code>/map</code>. HTTP:{" "}
        <code>GET /v1/sessions/&#123;id&#125;/workspace/map</code>.
        Capabilities: <code>workspace.repository_map</code> /{" "}
        <code>session.repository_map</code>. This is not a full semantic code
        index.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Adaptive compaction</h2>
      <p>
        When measured context grows large for an in-flight provider request,
        Veasel can compact extractively and emit a{" "}
        <code>session.compaction</code> event with measured bytes before/after.
        Optional summarizer:
      </p>
      <pre><code>VEASEL_SESSION_COMPACTION_SUMMARIZER=extractive   # default
VEASEL_SESSION_COMPACTION_SUMMARIZER=native       # structured local summary
VEASEL_SESSION_COMPACTION_SUMMARIZER=llm         # optional provider summary</code></pre>
      <p>
        LLM mode falls back on error, empty, or growth. Capability{" "}
        <code>session.compaction.summarizer</code> when enabled. Not
        provider-native compaction APIs; not invented cost. Details:{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/compatibility/session-compaction-summarizer.md">
          session-compaction-summarizer.md
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Prompt-cache accounting</h2>
      <p>
        When providers report cache read/write tokens, Veasel persists them (
        <code>sessions.usage.prompt_cache</code>) and surfaces them on{" "}
        <code>/usage</code> and operation resources. Anthropic Messages emit{" "}
        <code>cache_control</code> markers by default; OpenAI Chat/Responses
        emit <code>prompt_cache_key</code> by default for catalog endpoints —
        hits remain provider-reported only. No invented % savings.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Parallel read-only tools</h2>
      <p>
        Multi-tool rounds of workspace list/read/search run concurrently with
        ordered transcript append. Skill load, edits, shell, and MCP stay
        sequential. Mid-flight work interrupted by a restart is fail-closed as{" "}
        <code>uncertain</code> — never silently replayed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Cost schedule honesty</h2>
      <p>
        USD cost appears only when every reported turn matches the pinned
        schedule (embedded from <code>tools/cost-schedule/schedule.json</code>,
        overridable via env). Otherwise cost stays unavailable. Veasel does not
        invent prices, Harbor Index scores, or cross-agent rankings.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Durable async turns</h2>
      <p>
        Clients that send <code>Prefer: respond-async</code> get a durable
        operation ID (at most 32 queued rows per session). Queued turns resume
        after restart when the request, workspace, and model still validate.{" "}
        <code>autonomous:true</code> rows are not claimed unless the server
        opted in with <code>VEASEL_ALLOW_AUTONOMOUS_EXECUTION=1</code> (same
        gate as the HTTP turn path); otherwise they cancel without starting
        work. If the process dies after a worker claimed the turn, startup marks
        it <code>uncertain</code> and never replays provider calls or tool
        effects. Inspect the workspace before retrying.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Git worktrees</h2>
      <p>
        Manage linked worktrees for a session workspace through the local API or
        headless CLI. Listing reads the repository git directory (no{" "}
        <code>git</code> subprocess); add/remove/lock/unlock use argv-only{" "}
        <code>git worktree</code>.
      </p>
      <pre><code>veasel worktrees list
veasel worktrees add --path /abs/path --branch main
veasel worktrees add --path /abs/path --new-branch feature/x
veasel worktrees lock --path /abs/path --reason "hold review"
veasel worktrees unlock --path /abs/path
veasel worktrees remove --path /abs/path</code></pre>
      <p>
        HTTP under{" "}
        <code>/v1/sessions/&#123;id&#125;/workspace/git/worktrees</code>. Pass{" "}
        <code>--session</code> to reuse an existing session, or{" "}
        <code>--workspace</code> to create one.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/api/`}>
        API and headless <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/troubleshooting/`}>
        Troubleshooting <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
